  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM civil documentation Iraq</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IOM civil dokumentation Irak</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsens &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att adressera utmaningar och behov relaterade till tillg&#xe5;ng till identitetshandlingar (civil dokumentation) och r&#xe4;ttigheter g&#xe4;llande bostad, mark och egendom (HLP &#xac; Housing, land and property) f&#xf6;r &#xe5;terv&#xe4;ndare, internflyktingar, inklusive &#xe5;terv&#xe4;ndare fr&#xe5;n nord&#xf6;stra Syrien, milj&#xf6;migranter och v&#xe4;rdsamh&#xe4;llen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is to address challenges and needs related to access to identity documents (civil documentation) and rights concerning housing, land and property (HLP) for returnees, internally displaced persons &#x2014; including returnees from northeast Syria &#x2014; environmental migrants, and host communities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to address challenges related to access to identity documents and rights concerning housing, land, and property (HLP) for returnees, internally displaced persons (IDPs), environmental migrants, and host communities.

Objectives:

Improve access to legal support and reintegration for IDPs, returnees, migrants, and host communities.
Strengthen Iraqi authorities capacity to remove structural barriers and improve the issuance of civil documentation.
Key Outputs:

Legal and informational support for migrants, IDPs, and returnees, focusing on civil documentation, housing, land, and property rights.
Protection measures against gender-based violence and trafficking.
Capacity-building for Iraqi institutions involved in civil documentation and property rights.
Development of policies and support for Iraqs planning and implementation to enhance access to rights.</narrative>
  </description>
